      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals page: U2 PCA9685PW ... 'I2C address: 0x41'; A0 connected to +3.3V, A1-A5 connected to GND."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "If firmware expects the PWM driver at the specified address 0x40 on I2C2, it will not communicate with the servo/PWM driver; alternatively, if the spec is taken literally, this creates an address mismatch between intended and as-built hardware.",
      "confidence": 0.68
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The most clear deviation from the written specification is the PCA9685 PWM driver's configured I2C address: the schematic sets it to 0x41, while the specification states the intended address is 0x40. Other notable documented differences, such as the barometer RESET/INT mix-up, are explicitly listed in the spec as known limitations and were not treated as anomalies."
}

